<BaseLayout title="HT7 (Shenmen) — Spirit Gate Point" description="Learn how to locate and stimulate HT7 (Shenmen) — the Spirit Gate point. Benefits include insomnia relief, anxiety reduction, and heart calming." breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Points", href: "/points" }, { label: "HT7 (Shenmen)", href: "/points/ht7-shenmen-acupressure-point" }]} articleSchema={true}>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 lg:px-6">
    <h1 class="mb-4">HT7 (Shenmen) — Spirit Gate</h1>
    <p class="text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400 text-lg mb-8">HT7, known as Shenmen or Spirit Gate, is the source point of the Heart meridian. It is the primary point for calming the spirit, treating insomnia, anxiety, and heart palpitations.</p>

    <section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Location</h2>
    <img src="/images/ht7-location.webp" alt="HT7 acupressure point location on the inner wrist" class="w-full max-w-sm mx-auto rounded-xl shadow-sm" />
    <p class="mb-3">HT7 is located on the inner wrist, on the ulnar side (pinky side), at the proximal wrist crease. It lies in the depression just behind the pisiform bone, in line with the little finger.</p>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Benefits &amp; Uses</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-3 space-y-1 text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      <li><strong>Insomnia:</strong> HT7 promotes restful sleep and helps quiet a racing mind at bedtime.</li>
      <li><strong>Anxiety and panic:</strong> It reduces feelings of anxiety, nervousness, and panic attacks.</li>
      <li><strong>Heart palpitations:</strong> HT7 helps regulate heart rhythm and calms palpitations related to stress.</li>
      <li><strong>Emotional regulation:</strong> It stabilizes mood swings, irritability, and emotional sensitivity.</li>
      <li><strong>Mental clarity:</strong> HT7 improves focus and mental clarity by calming the mind.</li>
    </ul>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">How to Massage HT7</h2>
    <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2 text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      <li>Turn your hand so your palm faces upward.</li>
      <li>Place the thumb of your opposite hand on the HT7 point at the wrist crease.</li>
      <li>Apply gentle to moderate pressure in a small circular motion.</li>
      <li>Hold for 30?0 seconds, breathing slowly and deeply.</li>
      <li>Repeat on the other wrist as needed, especially before sleep.</li>
    </ol>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Science &amp; Research</h2>
    <p class="mb-3">A 2020 randomized controlled trial in <em>Journal of Clinical Nursing</em> found that HT7 acupressure significantly improved sleep quality in older adults with insomnia compared to sham treatment.<sup><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32077624/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">1</a></sup> Research in <em>BMC Complementary and Alternative Medicine</em> demonstrated that HT7 stimulation reduced anxiety scores in patients preparing for cardiac surgery.<sup><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30572886/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">2</a></sup></p>
    <p class="mb-3">A 2021 fMRI study in <em>Neuroscience Letters</em> showed that HT7 acupressure modulates the default mode network and limbic system, brain areas associated with emotional regulation and self-referential thought.<sup><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33964379/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">3</a></sup></p>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Precautions</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-3 space-y-1 text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      <li>Use gentle pressure ?the wrist area contains sensitive nerves and blood vessels.</li>
      <li>Avoid if you have a recent wrist injury, fracture, or carpal tunnel syndrome.</li>
      <li>Do not apply pressure if there are skin irritations, cuts, or rashes on the wrist.</li>
      <li>If you experience numbness or tingling in the hand, stop immediately.</li>
    </ul>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Related Points</h2>
    <p class="mb-3">HT7 pairs well with <a href="/points/pc6-neiguan-acupressure-point">PC6 (Neiguan)</a> for anxiety and palpitations. For insomnia, combine with <a href="/points/sp6-sanyinjiao-acupressure-point">SP6 (Sanyinjiao)</a> and <a href="/points/ki1-yongquan-acupressure-point">KI1 (Yongquan)</a>.</p>
  </section></article>
</BaseLayout>
